    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires `checkDigit` = a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode`, exposed on the owner response.\n\nChanges (kept structurally minimal \u2014 3 files, each change small and low-context):\n\n1. **`util/CheckDigits.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny cohesive utility with a single static `luhn(String)` method (null-safe, returns `Integer`). Isolating the loop in its own class means it carries no surrounding class complexity (`WMC_other` = 0).\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation on the existing `toOwnerDto` delegating to `CheckDigits.luhn(owner.getCustomerCode())`. No new logic inside any existing method; `toOwnerDto` itself has CC 1.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` schema field (integer 0\u20139, `readOnly`) to the owner response so the generated DTO carries the property.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes and `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
